      heading: "The tax registration number: yours, your customer's, and how to capture it",
      paragraphs: [
        `Your own registration number is a settings value that has to reach every document, including the ones nobody thinks about: the order confirmation email, the PDF attachment, the Arabic version of both, and whatever your booking system sends when a deposit is taken. We check all of those because the usual failure is a correct template and an email that still carries the demo text.`,
        `Your customer's number is the harder half, because a consumer does not have one and a business customer often will not type it unless asked at the right moment. The pattern that works is to split your checkout by customer type early, before payment, with a clear choice between buying as an individual and buying as a business. Choosing business reveals the fields the invoice will need: legal name as registered, registration number, and a structured address with the emirate from a list rather than typed.`,
        `Validate the format, because a number captured with spaces, dashes or a transposed digit is worse than an empty field: it produces a document that looks right and is wrong. UAE registration numbers have a fixed length, so a length and digit check at the point of entry catches most mistakes, and the authority publishes a verification tool your finance team can use for the ones that matter. Store the number exactly as validated, display it exactly as stored, and never let a later edit change it on an invoice that has already been issued.`,
      ],
